{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning, Mr. Thompson. I'm Dr. Reyes, one of your hospitalists. You're here today for your 32nd cycle of high-dose methotrexate, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, that's right. I was supposed to come in a few weeks ago, but I had a UTI, so they postponed it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see that in your chart. Good thing we waited — we don’t want to add infection risk during chemo. How have you been feeling otherwise?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Pretty stable. No headaches, no seizures, appetite’s good. Just this hip pain — been bothering me more lately."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see you’ve already had a right hip replacement. Is the pain on the other side?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, it’s the same right side. Not sure if it’s arthritis creeping in or just wear and tear. I’m hoping to schedule a revision soon, but I’m trying to time it between treatments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That makes sense. We’ll make sure your oncology team coordinates with ortho. For now, we’ll focus on getting your methotrexate in safely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I remember last time they gave me extra fluids and something to protect my kidneys?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We’ll start IV fluids with sodium bicarbonate to keep your urine alkaline — helps flush the methotrexate out and protects your kidneys. We’ll also monitor your levels closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And then leucovorin, right? To rescue me from the side effects?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll start leucovorin about 24 hours after the infusion ends. We’ll keep giving it until your methotrexate level drops below 0.1 — that’s when we know it’s safe to discharge you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And my seizures — I’m still on lamotrigine and topiramate. Should I keep taking them normally?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, absolutely. No changes there. Your neurologist wants you to stay on both. Any tremors or balance issues lately?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little shaky, especially when I walk heel-to-toe. But no falls. I’ve been careful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s good. That mild gait issue is known from your history — we’ll keep monitoring. Now, about your diabetes insipidus — you’re on desmopressin nasal spray, correct?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, twice a day. Sometimes I take an extra spray if I’m out and don’t want to keep running to the bathroom."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see that’s been a pattern. But when we give you lots of IV fluids, overusing desmopressin can drop your sodium too low. We’ll watch that closely — your level was 136 this morning, which is okay, but we don’t want it dropping."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I get it, but it’s hard. I don’t like being up all night peeing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. We’ll work with you — maybe adjust timing rather than dose. But for safety, we may need to hold an extra dose while you’re here on fluids."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2188-05-30 10:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Alright, I’ll cooperate. Just don’t want to feel lousy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2188-05-30 12:05:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi again. Your methotrexate infusion just finished — everything went smoothly. We’re continuing the bicarbonate IVs and will check your first level this evening."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2188-05-30 12:06:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That was it? Felt pretty normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2188-05-30 12:07:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Most patients don’t feel it during — side effects can come later, like nausea or fatigue. We’ve got anti-nausea meds on board if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2188-05-31 05:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your first methotrexate level came back at 5.5 — that’s expected this early. Your sodium dropped to 132, though."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2188-05-31 05:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that bad? I feel okay."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2188-05-31 05:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s mildly low. We think it’s because you used an extra desmopressin spray last night. We held the morning dose and will recheck sodium in a few hours."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2188-05-31 05:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did — I was tired and didn’t want to keep getting up. But I’ll stop if it’s risky."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2188-05-31 05:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We appreciate that. Your safety comes first. We’ll help you manage the bathroom trips when you’re home — maybe adjust timing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2188-05-31 18:20:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Update: your methotrexate level dropped to 0.22 — that’s great progress. One more dose of leucovorin tonight, and we’ll check again tomorrow morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2188-05-31 18:21:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So I might go home tomorrow?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2188-05-31 18:22:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We need the level below 0.1 and your sodium stable. We’re getting close."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news — your methotrexate level is now undetectable, and sodium is back to 134. We’ll discharge you today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great. What about my temozolomide? I usually start a new cycle around now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:27:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, you’re due for 7 days on, 7 off, then 7 on again. Keep taking it as usual — use Zofran if you feel nauseous."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:28:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my next methotrexate?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:29:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Scheduled in four months. Your oncology nurse will call to confirm the date."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:30:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I also have that MRI coming up — brain scan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:31:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, on June 15th at 1:45 PM with Dr. Lin. It’s to make sure your lymphoma remains in remission. No changes on the last one — that’s excellent."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:32:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Good. And my hip — should I see someone before scheduling surgery?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:33:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Talk to your oncologist first — they’ll clear you based on your counts and treatment schedule. Probably best to do it in the gap after your next methotrexate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:34:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I’ve been stressed with the divorce — hope it doesn’t affect my health."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:35:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Stress can take a toll. If you need support, we can connect you with counseling. Your propranolol can help with anxiety symptoms too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2188-06-01 05:36:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll keep that in mind. For now, I just want to get back to my routine."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2188-06-01 13:45:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re finalizing your discharge. You’ll go home on all your usual meds — desmopressin, lamotrigine, topiramate, lisinopril, and the temozolomide cycle as discussed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2188-06-01 13:46:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And no changes to the desmopressin?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2188-06-01 13:47:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Back to your usual dose — 2 sprays three times a day. But please don’t add extra. If you’re up at night, maybe take the last dose earlier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2188-06-01 13:48:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll try that. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2188-06-01 13:49:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll see you for the MRI, and your oncologist will follow up after that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2188-06-02 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just a final check-in before you leave. You’re doing well — alert, walking independently, no neurological issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2188-06-02 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Feeling ready to go home. Appreciate all the care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2188-06-02 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take it easy for a few days. Stay hydrated, but don’t overdo fluids. And call if you feel dizzy, confused, or have nausea that won’t stop."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2188-06-02 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. See you in four months — hopefully with better news about the hip."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2188-06-02 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Fingers crossed. Take care, Mr. Thompson."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2188-06-02 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks, Doctor."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2188-06-02 10:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Nurse will be in with your discharge paperwork and prescriptions shortly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2188-06-02 10:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. I’ll pack up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2188-06-02 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "One last thing — your urine pH was good during treatment, above 8, so your kidneys are protected. Great job staying on the bicarbonate."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2188-06-02 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Glad I could help. It wasn’t too bad."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2188-06-02 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Team effort. You’re cleared to go home now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2188-06-02 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thanks again. I’ll see you soon."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2188-06-02 12:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Safe travels home. Remember your MRI on the 15th — don’t miss it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2188-06-02 12:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "On my calendar."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2188-06-02 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Final check — all labs stable, you’re alert, and walking well. Discharge is official."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2188-06-02 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Appreciate it. I’ll follow up as planned."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2188-06-02 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, Mr. Thompson."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2188-06-02 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "You too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2188-06-02 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Just confirming — you have a ride home and someone to check in on you tonight?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 68,
      "time": "2188-06-02 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, my son’s picking me up and staying tonight."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 69,
      "time": "2188-06-02 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Perfect. Call us if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 70,
      "time": "2188-06-02 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will do. Thanks for everything."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2188-05-30 10:11:00",
    "admission_end": "2188-06-02 14:00:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 65-year-old man with a history of CNS B-cell lymphoma and diabetes insipidus was admitted for his 32nd cycle of high-dose methotrexate chemotherapy. The infusion was completed without complications, and he received leucovorin rescue starting 24 hours later. Methotrexate levels decreased appropriately, falling to undetectable by discharge. Mild hyponatremia (sodium 132) was noted, attributed to overuse of desmopressin in the setting of aggressive hydration, and was discussed with the patient. He remained neurologically stable with no seizures or focal deficits. Temozolomide was restarted per outpatient regimen. He was discharged home in stable condition with instructions to continue all medications, attend a follow-up brain MRI, and schedule his next methotrexate in four months.",
    "problems": [
      "Encounter for antineoplastic chemotherapy",
      "Unspecified B-cell lymphoma, extranodal and solid organ sites",
      "Diabetes insipidus",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Unspecified osteoarthritis, unspecified site",
      "Personal history of nicotine dependence"
    ]
  }
}
